    "message": "fix(view): say the port is unknown from status, not nothing\n\nReview follow-up. `ix view` and `ix view status` disagreed in exactly the\nstate that motivated #358: with a live PID but no recoverable port, `ix view`\nprinted the \"port is unknown\" advisory and told you how to recover, while\n`status` printed the PID line and stopped.\n\nNeither guessed a URL, so this was never a #358 regression -- but silence is\nthe wrong answer for someone who ran `status` *for* the URL, and it was also\nunpinned: the existing test only asserted the absence of \"http://localhost\",\nwhich the advisory satisfies too, so the behaviour could drift either way.\n\nRoute status through runningInstanceLines so the two branches cannot drift.\n`status` takes no -p, so the mismatch branch is unreachable from here.\n\nConfirmed non-vacuous: with the old two-line form restored, the new test fails\non \"expected '[ok] Visualizer is running (PID 4242)' to contain 'unknown'\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PZhcNcCtFQ6Bz2XMDpJPJS",
